speechtext:
1 bo 4. No permanent appointments have been made. The following positions have been established in connection with the new public building: 1 public building engineer caretaker;
1	stationary engineer of heating, grade 2;
2	elevator operators; 6 cleaners and helpers; 1 watchman; 2 firemen-labouters; 1 seasonal fireman; 1 charwoman.
The appointment of a caretaker, engineer, five cleaners and helpers, watchman and two elevator operators will be made by the Civil Sendee Commission. The position of caretaker, engineer and cleaners and helpers are now being advertised by the Civil Service Commission. Appointments to the remaining positions will be made by the Department of Public Works.

I have given my ruling;
if any hon. member wishes to appeal therefrom he may do so.
Motion dropped.
